hermes v0.23.0: vision for every main model, whatever the image's source
(chat upload, downloaded file, browser screenshot).

Three problems, one patch (all three decide whether a session sees images):

1. agent/image_routing.py decide_image_input_mode(): an explicit
   `auxiliary.vision` backend (provider other than auto, or a model or
   base_url) forced the text-description path for EVERY main model,
   including vision-capable ones. So configuring a describer for the
   text-only models (GLM on OpenRouter, whose auto route finds none:
   _vision_auto_route skips the main provider as text-only and then
   skips OpenRouter as "already tried") took native pixels away from
   Claude. Now the explicit backend is the describer for main models that
   cannot see; a model the capability lookup attests as vision-capable
   stays native. `agent.image_input_mode: text` still forces the
   description path for everyone.

2. Camofox's browser_vision always described the screenshot through the
   auxiliary model, never native. Since v0.23.0 Camofox is the official
   `camofox` plugin, so that fix lives in hyperhermes'
   pkgs/hermes-camofox-plugin/native-vision.patch; this patch makes the
   gate it uses (_should_use_native_vision_fast_path) per main model.

3. tools/registry.py _check_fn_cached() and model_tools.py
   _tool_defs_cache_key(): both caches were keyed by function and profile
   only, but check_vision_requirements() answers per main model (native
   fast path or a vision backend for it). In one gateway, a turn of a
   text-only model without a vision backend cached False, and the next
   session on Claude got a tool list without vision_analyze and
   browser_vision (and the reverse: the text-only model was offered a
   vision_analyze that then failed with "No LLM provider configured for
   task=vision"). Both keys now include the main provider+model
   (main_runtime_cache_key: set_runtime_main()'s context, else
   config.yaml).

Upstream status: not reported upstream yet; unchanged in v0.23.0. Since
v0.23.0 the tool-list key also carries upstream's check_fn_cache_epoch();
the main-model element sits next to it (both are needed: the epoch voids
the lists of dropped verdicts, the model separates per-model verdicts).
Also fixes the docstring of tools/vision_tools.py
_native_tool_result_images, which named the explicit backend as a reason
for text.

